profile: mirust.talisman-source.totem.v2
updated_utc: 2026-08-28T00:00:00Z
site: MiRust.com
role: positive_anchor
mission: Preserve the Rust-family identity for local-first model runtimes, checksum-bound evidence, peer/local model agency, and UAIX-style memory discipline.
anchors:
  - Rust-first engineering with explicit boundaries.
  - Browser-local or user-local model execution unless a human creates a separate reviewed service boundary.
  - Checksum-bearing provenance for model packages, evidence, reports, and durable memory.
  - File Handoff intake must be reviewed, dispositioned, recorded, and cleared after processing.
  - Client sites may look up to MiRust.com for talisman posture while retaining local ownership.
agent_mutability: read_only_without_exact_human_artifact_and_operation_authorization

pre_publication_clean_slate_policy_id: pre-publication-clean-slate-v1
pre_publication_clean_slate_authority: "Treat this site and every consuming system as pre-publication dogfood, even when a development URL is publicly reachable. Until the human explicitly removes this authority, choose the best current architecture; full rewrites and clean contract replacements are authorized when they improve correctness, security, maintainability, performance, accessibility, or product quality."
pre_publication_replacement_completion_authority: "Verify replacements end to end, migrate every dogfood caller to one current contract, remove superseded implementation in the same completed change, and finish tests, documentation, security review, and cleanup before deployment. Preserve immutable receipts and historical failure evidence as audit truth, never as a promise to support obsolete product behavior."
documentation_integrity_policy_id: site-family-documentation-integrity-v1
documentation_site_role: documentation-evidence-marketing-architecture-research-and-governance-authority
documentation_integrity_authority: "Documentation is a first-class production surface and a primary function of this site. Keep architecture, governance, research synthesis, evidence boundaries, product relationships, security, privacy, accessibility, limitations, and release material complete, technically rigorous, navigable, searchable, and current."
documentation_same_change_rule: "Update every affected page, example, diagram, claim, cross-site link, version reference, update history entry, and machine-readable release record in the same completed change as the product, contract, governance, or evidence change it describes."
documentation_verification_rule: "Before publication, verify sources and claim scope, examples, links, navigation, search discoverability, accessibility, responsive rendering, version consistency, and public HTTPS readback across the full affected documentation closure."
documentation_truth_rule: "Clearly distinguish research, proposal, implementation, local test, independent proof, deployment, limitation, rejection, and blocker. Marketing language must never outrun objective evidence or the authoritative product and documentation sites."
documentation_release_gate: "Do not publish an affected site when documentation is incomplete, stale, contradictory, unsupported, version-skewed, unverified, or inconsistent with related sites and release evidence."
documentation_clean_replacement_rule: "Remove superseded guidance and claims after verified replacement. Preserve immutable release history and failure evidence separately; do not retain obsolete instructions or descriptions as legacy support."
memory_endpoints_policy_id: memory-endpoints-two-lane-ecosystem-v1
memory_endpoints_agent_coordination_use: "Agents working on all ecosystem sites use MemoryEndpoints.com directly for agent-to-agent long-term memory, meetings, handoffs, and coordination."
memory_endpoints_tinyrustlm_connect_use: "Separately, the TinyRustLM.com Connect plugin lets a user sign in to MemoryEndpoints.com and explicitly use it as the long-term-memory provider for TinyRustLM.com Connect."
memory_endpoints_lane_boundary: "Keep direct agent coordination and the user plugin separately identified, scoped, consented, authenticated, and evidenced; neither lane silently grants authority to the other, and configured or reachable state is not live-operation proof."
memory_redundancy_rule: "During prelaunch, important memory may also be retained in current .uai, wiki, source-controlled public-safe notes, or other approved stores for resilience. Every maintained copy must stay current, provenance-labeled, secret-safe, and noncontradictory."
